---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro'

const DESCRIPTION =
  'What Wiracocha Labs receives through this site and its WhatsApp channel, what we use it ' +
  'for, who else sees it, and how to get it deleted.'
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy — Wiracocha Labs"
  description={DESCRIPTION}
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="November 13, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This project does not run on your data. This page says exactly what we receive, why, and how
    to get it deleted — short, and without fine print.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Wiracocha Labs is an open research project run by Renzo Tincopa, an individual based in
    Urubamba, Cusco, Peru. For anything about your data, write to
    <a href="mailto:wiracochalabs@protonmail.com">wiracochalabs@protonmail.com</a>. That address
    reaches the only person who can act on it.
  </p>

  <h2>What this covers</h2>
  <p>
    This website (wiracochalabs.com) and the WhatsApp channel linked from our Instagram profile.
    If you reach us through another channel, that channel&rsquo;s own rules apply.
  </p>

  <h2>What we receive</h2>
  <p>Only what you send us.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>On WhatsApp:</strong> your phone number, the name on your profile, the content and
      time of your messages, and delivery information (whether it arrived, whether it was read).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>By email:</strong> your address and whatever you write in the message.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Nothing else. No location, no access to your contacts, no payment data. We do not ask for
    those. Please do not send sensitive data (health, financial, identity documents) through the
    chat — if it arrives anyway, we delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we never do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We do not sell, rent or trade your data. Not to advertisers, not to anyone.
    </li>
    <li>
      We do not build profiles, score people, or create advertising audiences.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We do not write to you first.</strong> We answer what you send. We only contact you
      outside the conversation if you explicitly ask us to in the chat, and we keep a record of
      that request.
    </li>
    <li>
      No mailing list, no analytics, no advertising pixels, no social trackers on this site.
    </li>
    <li>
      No automated decisions about you: the bot answers questions, it does not decide anything
      about your rights.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The replies are automated</h2>
  <p>
    The WhatsApp channel is answered by a bot, not by a person. A bot can be wrong: treat its
    answers as a starting point, not as an offer, a quote, or professional advice. When you ask
    for a person, we reply ourselves.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>
    Your messages pass through three providers. None of them may use your data for their own
    purposes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Meta / WhatsApp</strong> (WhatsApp Business Platform): receives and delivers the
      message. Governed by
      <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        WhatsApp&rsquo;s privacy policy</a
      >
      and its
      <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/business-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        business terms</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>ManyChat</strong>: the automation platform that runs the bot. It stores the
      conversation, your phone number and the fields the bot captures, on servers in the United
      States, under its
      <a href="https://manychat.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        own privacy policy</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong>: serves this website and keeps technical logs (IP address, date,
      page requested) for security and uptime. See
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Cloudflare&rsquo;s privacy policy</a
      >.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>International transfer</h2>
  <p>
    Meta and ManyChat process this data in the United States. Writing to us means accepting that
    transfer: it is how these platforms work, and there is no version of this channel that keeps
    the data inside Peru.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    One year from your last message if nothing moves forward. After that, we delete it. If we end
    up working together, we keep it for the length of the project plus what the law requires
    (accounting records, for example). Nothing is kept &ldquo;just in case&rdquo;.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to show you what we hold, correct it, delete it, stop using it, or take back
    your consent. Write to
    <a href="mailto:wiracochalabs@protonmail.com">wiracochalabs@protonmail.com</a> and say what you
    need. You do not have to explain why.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with our answer, you can go to the National Authority for Personal
    Data Protection (ANPD) at the Ministry of Justice and Human Rights of Peru.
  </p>

  <h2 id="deletion">Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>This is a commitment, not a vague gesture.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Send the word &ldquo;delete&rdquo; in the WhatsApp chat, or email us, and tell us what to
      remove.
    </li>
    <li>
      Within <strong>7 business days</strong> we confirm by email what was deleted and on what
      date. Give us an email address in the chat and that email is your receipt.
    </li>
    <li>
      We delete the copy stored in ManyChat and the conversation history held by the bot. The one
      copy we cannot delete is the one Meta keeps under its own policy — you can request that
      directly from WhatsApp.
    </li>
    <li>
      The only thing we keep is what the law obliges us to keep, such as accounting records.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Removing published content</h2>
  <p>
    If you own something published on this site — a logo, an image, a text — and you want it
    taken down, write to the same email. It comes off as soon as we confirm you are the owner,
    normally the same day. Search engines and saved copies can take a few days to catch up; that
    part is out of our hands.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Keeping little data, for a short time, is the best protection there is. Access is limited to
    one person, with two-factor authentication on the accounts involved. Nobody can promise
    absolute security, and we will not pretend to. If something happens that may affect you, we
    tell you.
  </p>

  <h2>Minors</h2>
  <p>
    This channel is for people hiring or evaluating services. We do not knowingly collect data
    from minors. If you think we hold data from a minor, tell us and we delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If something changes, we update the date at the top. The version published here is the one
    that counts.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
